  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "This distance between the 2 successive lines (wavefronts) is <math> <mi>λ</mi> </math>. This is for both the straight and curved lines.<br /><br />So, wavefront XY is separated by a distance of <math> <mrow> <mn>3</mn><mi>λ</mi></mrow> </math> from the wavefront that has reached point P.<br /><br />Distance that needs to be traveled<math> <mrow> <mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>λ</mi></mrow> </math><br /><br />Speed of light <math> <mrow> <mo>=</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow> </math><br /><br />Speed = Distance/Time<br /><br />Time = distance/speed <math> <mrow> <mo>=</mo><mfrac> <mrow> <mn>3</mn><mi>λ</mi></mrow> <mi>c</mi> </mfrac> </mrow> </math>",
    "image": null
